syntax: a recovered case item without patterns has no position

With RecoverErrors, a case item cut off before its first pattern, as in
"case x in (" or "case x in a) ;; (" at the end of the input, is kept
without patterns. CaseItem.Pos indexed Patterns[0], so walking such a
tree and asking a node for its position panicked with an index out of
range. Such an item now reports an invalid position, as other recovered
nodes do.

Reproducer, before this change: parse "case x in (" with RecoverErrors(3)
and call Pos on every node Walk visits; it panics.

diff --git a/syntax/nodes.go b/syntax/nodes.go
index d0ad7f5..8a625e5 100644
--- a/syntax/nodes.go
+++ b/syntax/nodes.go
@@ -1055,7 +1055,14 @@ type CaseItem struct {
 	Last  []Comment
 }
 
-func (c *CaseItem) Pos() Pos { return c.Patterns[0].Pos() }
+func (c *CaseItem) Pos() Pos {
+	if len(c.Patterns) == 0 {
+		// Only error recovery leaves an item without patterns, such as
+		// at the end of "case x in (".
+		return Pos{}
+	}
+	return c.Patterns[0].Pos()
+}
 func (c *CaseItem) End() Pos {
 	if c.OpPos.IsValid() {
 		return posAddCol(c.OpPos, len(c.Op.String()))
